# Language Policy for Control Artifacts

The meta/steering layer of this repo is written in **English** so it stays environment- and team-neutral. Content planning documents stay in the language the user chose for them.

## Rule

| Artifact | Language |
|---|---|
| Rules (`.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc`) | **always English** |
| `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` | **always English** |
| Skills (`.agents/skills/**/SKILL.md`) | **always English** |
| Code & code comments | **always English** |
| Tracker content (title, description, comments, worklog) | **always English** |
| Planning / output docs (`docs/tasks/**`, other deliverables) | **the language the user picks** — the repo's default is a value: the target repo's `AGENTS.md` → key `Doc language` |

## Scope vs. `general-english-comments`

This rule is the **superset**: it governs the language of *all* steering artifacts (rules, skills, entry files, code). The narrower rule `general-english-comments` covers **only code comments** and defers to this rule for everything else. There is no overlap: one canonical owner per aspect.

- Translating a planning doc into the tracker is allowed and goes **only** repo → tracker, never back.
- A control artifact (rule, skill, entry file) must never be authored or left in a language other than English.
